<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 5.023 billion pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 5.023 billion pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 5.023 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Dealers added the central bank intended to drain liquidity through four secondary auctions, which it offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    1.000 bln  7 days    25.27 pct</p>
<p>1.000 bln  6 days</p>
<p>1.400 bln  5 days</p>
<p>1.623 bln  3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
